<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6200" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμωμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>blameless,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Semon.
				4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.177
				</span></i>
			; <i>without blemish,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶδος ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					259
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλλει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					185
				</span></i>
			; in epitaphs, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				1974
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Thessalonica</span>), al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>unblemished,</i> of victims, etc., <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				29.1
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ep.Pet.</u>
				1.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.171
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>unimpaired, perfect,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑγίεια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					5(1).1119
				</span></i>
			 (Geronthrae, <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>).</div>
